The '''2026–27 Malaysia Super League'''(also known as the 2026–27 '''Unifi Liga Super''' for sponsorship reasons) ({{langx|ms|Liga Super Malaysia 2026–27}}) will be the 23rd season of the [[Malaysia Super League]], the top-tier professional [[association football|football]] league in [[Malaysia]] since its establishment in 2004, and the 45th season of the top-flight [[Malaysian football league system|Malaysian football]] overall.

[[Johor Darul Ta'zim F.C.|Johor Darul Ta'zim]] are the defending champions, having won their record 12th Super League title in the previous season.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.thestar.com.my/sport/football/2026/03/15/jdt-clinch-12th-super-league-title|website=thestar|title=JDT clinch 12th Super League title|date=15 Mar 2026}}</ref>

==Teams==
===Changes from the previous season===
A total of twelve teams are confirmed to contest the league, including eleven from the [[2025–26 Malaysia Super League|2025–26 season]], one promoted from the [[2025–26 Malaysia A1 Semi-Pro League|A1 Semi-Pro League]]. Kelantan Red Warrior will play in the Super League for the first time in their history.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.tvsarawak.my/2026/07/16/kelantan-red-warrior-sah-ke-liga-super/|title=Kelantan Red Warrior sah ke Liga Super|date=16 July 2026|publisher=tvsarawak|website=tvsarawak.com}}</ref> Kelantan The Real Warriors and PDRM were ejected from Super League due to failure to obtain a national license. Immigration FC rebranded to [[Star City F.C.|Star City]] for this season.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.flashsukan.com.my/imigresen-fc-kini-dikenali-sebagai-star-city-fc/|title=Imigresen FC Kini Dikenali Sebagai Star City FC|date=1 July 2026|publisher=flashsukan|website=flashsukan.com}}</ref>

